    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d168">

                <pb facs="0300" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.01 Bills/9–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Commissioner in India</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Merrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-28T21:00:00-04:00">September 28,
                            1945—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>768. House Rules Committee on Sept. 26 recommended to House that preferred
                    treatment on calender be given to Indian Immigration Bill.</p>
                <pb facs="0301" n="289" xml:id="pg289"/>
                <p>For your confidential information, House is not likely to debate measure before
                    Oct. 10<anchor n="96" xml:id="d168-f1"/> as several members favorably disposed
                    to bill will be in Europe until that date.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d168-f1" n="96" xml:id="d168-f1-content">
                <p>The bill, H.R. 3517, was debated and passed by the House of Representatives on
                    October 10; its legislative history extended to June 1946, at which time the
                    Senate passed an amended version of the House bill on June 14, a Conference
                    settlement being effected on June 29, 1946 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Congressional Record</hi>, vol. 91, pt. 7, p. 9544; vol. 92, pt. 6, pp.
                    6543, 6918, 6933, 7077, and 7957). The bill was approved by President Truman on
                    July 2, 1946 (60 Stat. 416).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
